message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Baseball Research Lab: a pitch-level MLB simulator with a registered research ledger and a hitter-pitcher matchup report"
authors:
  - family-names: Greenblatt
    given-names: Alec
repository-code: "https://github.com/AlecGreenblatt36/Pitcher-Research-Lab"
url: "https://alecgreenblatt36.github.io/Pitcher-Research-Lab/"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-09"
keywords:
  - baseball
  - simulation
  - forecasting
  - swing decisions
  - preregistration
abstract: "An MLB game simulator (seven-outcome plate-appearance model, pitch-level engine, Monte Carlo) with a public forecast record, and a matchup report that prices where to pitch each hitter from his own swing map read at the decision moment. Every experiment is registered in LEDGER.md before it runs, with its prediction, result and decision, including the failed ones; the pricing of the aiming edge was stress-tested in synthetic seasons with known truth before it was stated."
